content.text:
I have a complete picture. Here is the full report.

---

# 1. Editor engine

**Tiptap v3 on ProseMirror.** From `/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/package.json` (`dependencies`), all pinned at `^3.22.4` unless noted:

```
@tiptap/core                 ^3.22.4
@tiptap/pm                   ^3.22.4
@tiptap/starter-kit          ^3.22.4
@tiptap/extension-highlight  ^3.22.4
@tiptap/extension-image      ^3.22.4
@tiptap/extension-link       ^3.22.4
@tiptap/extension-placeholder ^3.22.4
@tiptap/extension-subscript  3.22.4   (exact)
@tiptap/extension-superscript 3.22.4  (exact)
@tiptap/extension-table      ^3.22.4
@tiptap/extension-table-cell / -header / -row  ^3.22.4
@tiptap/extension-task-item / -task-list       ^3.22.4
@tiptap/extension-text-align ^3.22.4
@tiptap/extension-text-style 3.22.4   (exact)
@tiptap/extension-typography ^3.22.4
@tiptap/extension-underline  ^3.22.4
```

No lexical, no slate. Framework is **Qwik 2** (`@qwik.dev/core@2.0.0-beta.42`) — this matters enormously for section 2. Tailwind v4 via `@tailwindcss/vite`.

## Editor instantiation

`/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/src/components/editor/twyne-editor.tsx:688` — `new Editor({...})` inside a `useVisibleTask$`. The mount element is looked up by id at line 490:

```ts
// twyne-editor.tsx:490
const el = document.getElementById("twyne-editor-mount");
if (!el) {
  console.warn("[twyne:editor] #twyne-editor-mount not found in DOM");
```

### Full extension list (`twyne-editor.tsx:691-770`)

| Extension | Config |
|---|---|
| `StarterKit` | `heading: { levels: [1,2,3] }`, `link: false`, `underline: false` |
| `ImageNode` (custom) | `uploadAdapter`, `onUploadError` |
| `...createTableCoreExtensions({ resizable: true })` | Table/Row/Header/Cell |
| `TableCellFormat` (custom) | |
| `Placeholder` | `"Begin writing from the brief. The room of editors is listening..."` |
| `Highlight` | `multicolor: true` |
| `Underline`, `Subscript`, `Superscript` | |
| `TextStyleKit` | `lineHeight: false` |
| `TextAlign` | `types: ["heading","paragraph"]`, 4 alignments |
| `TiptapLink` | `openOnClick: true`, `autolink: true`, class `editor-link` |
| `Typography` | |
| `TaskList` / `TaskItem` | `nested: true` |
| `CommentMark`, `PersonaNoteMark`, `SuggestionMark` | custom marks |
| `MermaidDiagram`, `InlineNoteNode` | custom nodes |
| `RemoteCursors` | `{ cursors: [] }` |
| `MarkAnchorWidgets`, `Indent`, `FindReplace`, `SlashCommand` | custom |
| `...MathExtensions` | |
| **`SectionReorder`** | **custom drag extension — see §2** |
| `ParagraphFormat`, `PageBreakNode` | |
| `Pagination` | `layout`, `getTailElement: () => document.querySelector(".manuscript-notes")`, `onPaginate` |

**StarterKit defaults that remain ON** (verified in `node_modules/@tiptap/starter-kit/dist/index.js:42-88`):

```js
import { Dropcursor, Gapcursor, TrailingNode, UndoRedo } from "@tiptap/extensions";
...
if (this.options.dropcursor !== false) extensions.push(Dropcursor.configure(this.options.dropcursor));
if (this.options.gapcursor  !== false) extensions.push(Gapcursor.configure(this.options.gapcursor));
if (this.options.trailingNode !== false) extensions.push(TrailingNode.configure(...));
```

Only `link` and `underline` are disabled, so **Dropcursor, Gapcursor, TrailingNode, UndoRedo, ListKeymap are all active.**

### editorProps — the complete set (`twyne-editor.tsx:772-800`)

```ts
editorProps: {
  attributes: {
    class: "ProseMirror",
  },
  handleDrop: (view, event, _slice, moved) => {
    if (moved) return false;
    const coords = { left: event.clientX, top: event.clientY };
    const pos = view.posAtCoords(coords);
    if (!pos) return false;

    const html = event.dataTransfer?.getData("text/html");
    if (html) {
      if (html.includes("<table") || html.includes("<img")) {
        const tempDiv = document.createElement("div");
        tempDiv.innerHTML = html;
        const img = tempDiv.querySelector("img");
        if (img?.src) {
          const node = view.state.schema.nodes.image.create({
            src: img.src,
            alt: img.alt || "",
          });
          const tr = view.state.tr.insert(pos.pos, node);
          view.dispatch(tr);
          return true;
        }
      }
    }

    return false;
  },
},
onUpdate: ({ editor: e }) => { scheduleLiveMeta(e); scheduleDerive(e); },
```

**There is no `handleKeyDown`, no `handleDOMEvents`, no `handleClick`, no `handlePaste` in `editorProps`.** A repo-wide grep confirms only three files declare PM prop handlers at all:

```
src/components/editor/extensions/section-reorder.ts:222:  handleDOMEvents: {
src/components/editor/extensions/image-node.ts:658:  handlePaste: ...
src/components/editor/twyne-editor.tsx:772:  editorProps: {
```

Note `attributes.class = "ProseMirror"` is redundant (PM sets it anyway) but harmless.

---

# 2. Drag and drop — the core findings

## 2a. Dropcursor / Gapcursor

- **Dropcursor: ENABLED** (StarterKit default, not disabled).
- **Gapcursor: ENABLED** (StarterKit default) — **but its CSS is missing.** `node_modules/@tiptap/extensions/dist/index.js:185` shows Gapcursor is a bare plugin wrapper with no style injection:
  ```js
  var Gapcursor = Extension4.create({
    name: "gapCursor",
    addProseMirrorPlugins() { return [gapCursor()]; },
    extendNodeSchema(extension) { ... allowGapCursor ... }
  });
  ```
  A repo-wide grep for `ProseMirror-gapcursor` returns **zero hits** in `src/`. `prosemirror-gapcursor/style/gapcursor.css` is never imported. So the gap cursor is functionally active but **invisible** — the writer gets no caret when they click into a gap before/after an atom node (image, math, mermaid, page break, endnote).

## 2b. The three drag systems, layered on one another

### (i) Qwik `preventdefault:` on the scroll container — the biggest suspect

`/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/src/components/editor/manuscript-panel.tsx:42-51`, verbatim:

```tsx
      <div
        class="flex-1 overflow-y-auto overflow-x-auto"
        style="background: var(--color-editor-bg);"
        preventdefault:dragover
        preventdefault:dragleave
        preventdefault:drop
        onDragOver$={props.onDragOver$}
        onDragLeave$={props.onDragLeave$}
        onDrop$={props.onDrop$}
      >
```

This div is the **ancestor of the entire ProseMirror DOM** (`#twyne-editor-mount` is nested inside it at line 102).

**Critical mechanism:** Qwik registers its delegated listeners on the document in the **capture phase**, and calls `preventDefault()` *before* the event ever reaches ProseMirror. From `node_modules/@qwik.dev/core/dist/qwikloader.debug.js`:

```js
// line 379 — note the 4th arg `true` = capture
roots.forEach((root) => addEventListener(root, eventName, processElementEvent, true, passive));

// line ~28 — signature
var addEventListener = (el, eventName, handler, capture = false, passive = false) =>
    el.addEventListener(eventName, handler, { capture, passive });

// line 150 — inside dispatch(), walking target → ancestors
if (allowPreventDefault && element.hasAttribute("preventdefault:" + kebabName)) ev.preventDefault();
```

So on **every** `dragover`, `dragleave`, and `drop` anywhere inside the manuscript, `event.preventDefault()` fires at document-capture, ahead of `view.dom`'s handlers, ahead of Dropcursor, ahead of `SectionReorder.handleDOMEvents`, ahead of `editorProps.handleDrop`.

For `dragover` this is benign-to-helpful (it's how you mark a drop target). For **`drop` it cancels the browser's native drop default for the whole subtree** — and it's applied unconditionally to text-selection drags, file drags, everything.

### (ii) The `.drag-overlay` fires on internal text drags

`twyne-editor.tsx:2450-2460`:

```ts
    const handleDragOver = $(() => {
      store.isDragOver = true;
    });

    const handleDragLeave = $(() => {
      store.isDragOver = false;
    });

    const handleDrop = $(() => {
      store.isDragOver = false;
    });
```

Wired at `twyne-editor.tsx:3244-3246`. There is **no filtering on `dataTransfer.types`** — dragging a text selection inside the manuscript sets `isDragOver = true`, which renders (`manuscript-panel.tsx:52-56`):

```tsx
        {store.isDragOver && (
          <div class="drag-overlay">
            <span>Drop plate or tabular here</span>
          </div>
        )}
```

`src/global.css:1458-1470`:

```css
/* Drag-over overlay */
.drag-overlay {
  position: fixed;
  inset: 0;
  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-vermilion) 7%, transparent);
  border: 2px dashed var(--color-vermilion);
  z-index: var(--z-overlay);
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  pointer-events: none;
}
```

`pointer-events: none` means it does **not** block the drop — good. But it is `position: fixed; inset: 0`, covering the viewport, and it appears the moment you start dragging selected text, announcing "Drop plate or tabular here". Worse: `dragleave` fires every time the pointer crosses an element boundary, so `isDragOver` flips true/false continuously during a drag, causing a Qwik re-render storm mid-drag over the ProseMirror-managed DOM.

### (iii) `SectionReorder` — custom block drag handles on every heading

`/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/src/components/editor/extensions/section-reorder.ts`. The whole file is drag code; the load-bearing parts:

**Handle widget (lines 40-53)** — a `draggable=true` widget decoration injected before *every* heading:

```ts
function dragHandle(id: string, label: string): HTMLElement {
  const handle = document.createElement("span");
  handle.dataset.sectionDragHandle = id;
  handle.draggable = true;
  handle.contentEditable = "false";
  handle.className = "twyne-section-drag-handle";
  handle.setAttribute("role", "button");
  handle.setAttribute("aria-label", `Move section: ${label}`);
  handle.setAttribute("title", `Drag to move ${label}`);
  handle.textContent = "⋮⋮";
  handle.style.cssText =
    "position:absolute;transform:translate(-1.5rem,.2rem);cursor:grab;user-select:none;opacity:.55;";
  return handle;
}
```

Placed at line 60-69 via `Decoration.widget(heading.from, ..., { side: -1, key: ... })`, using `buildDocumentOutline(doc).flat` — which includes **h1 through h6** (`src/utils/document-outline.ts:4-5`, `MIN_HEADING_LEVEL = 1`).

Note: `.twyne-section-drag-handle` has **no CSS rule anywhere in the repo** — all styling is the inline `cssText` above. That's the only `user-select: none` in any editor component.

**`handleDOMEvents` (lines 222-325):**

```ts
handleDOMEvents: {
  dragstart(view, event) {
    const handle = eventElement(event)?.closest<HTMLElement>("[data-section-drag-handle]");
    const sourceId = handle?.dataset.sectionDragHandle;
    if (!sourceId) return false;          // ← native text drag falls through, OK
    event.dataTransfer?.setData(SECTION_DRAG_MIME, sourceId);
    if (event.dataTransfer) event.dataTransfer.effectAllowed = "move";
    view.dispatch(...dragStart meta...);
    return true;
  },
  dragover(view, event) {
    const pluginState = sectionReorderPluginKey.getState(view.state);
    if (!pluginState?.draggingId) return false;   // ← gates on section drag, OK
    const hovered = headingAtEvent(view, event);
    if (!hovered) return false;
    ...
    event.preventDefault();
    if (event.dataTransfer) event.dataTransfer.dropEffect = "move";
    ...
    return true;
  },
  drop(view, event) {
    const pluginState = sectionReorderPluginKey.getState(view.state);
    const sourceId =
      pluginState?.draggingId ||
      event.dataTransfer?.getData(SECTION_DRAG_MIME);
    const hovered = headingAtEvent(view, event);
    if (!sourceId || !hovered) return false;
    // DOM event handlers do not implicitly cancel browser behavior.
    // Cancel before validation so an invalid self-drop cannot insert
    // the draggable widget's text into the editable manuscript.
    event.preventDefault();
    ...
    return true;
  },
  dragend(view) {
    clearDrag(view);
    return false;
  },
},
```

The gating is correct in principle (`return false` lets PM's native text-drag path run). But note `dragend` dispatches a transaction on *every* drag end, including plain text drags — `clearDrag` always fires `view.dispatch(...)`.

**`headingAtEvent` (lines 101-134) — relevant to your H1 suspicion:**

```ts
  const atCoords = view.posAtCoords({ left: event.clientX, top: event.clientY });
  if (!atCoords) return null;
  let target = outline.flat[0];              // ← defaults to the FIRST heading
  for (const heading of outline.flat) {
    if (heading.from > atCoords.pos) break;
    target = heading;
  }
```

Any drop whose coordinates resolve *before* the first heading still snaps to `outline.flat[0]` — i.e. the document's H1. Combined with the `dropPlacement` midpoint test (lines 136-144), a drop in the top region of the document always targets the H1.

### (iv) Node-level `draggable` flags

```
src/components/editor/extensions/image-node.ts:561:  draggable: true,     // ImageNode, atom + isolating
src/components/editor/extensions/image-node.ts:374:  this.image.draggable = false;   // inner <img> in the NodeView
src/components/editor/extensions/mermaid-node.ts:28:  draggable: true,
src/components/editor/extensions/math.ts:293:  draggable: true,
src/components/editor/extensions/page-break-node.ts:39:  draggable: false,
src/components/editor/extensions/section-reorder.ts:43:  handle.draggable = true,
```

### (v) `image-node.ts` drop handling (lines 638-657)

```ts
          handleDrop: (view, event, _slice, moved) => {
            if (moved) return false;
            const files = imageFilesFromList(event.dataTransfer?.files);
            if (files.length === 0) return false;
            event.preventDefault();
            const at = view.posAtCoords({ left: event.clientX, top: event.clientY });
            insertImageFiles(this.editor, files, adapter, at?.pos, onUploadError);
            return true;
          },
```

Correctly gated on `moved` and on actual files.

## 2c. CSS that could block dragging

- **`-webkit-user-drag`: zero occurrences anywhere in `src/`.**
- **`user-select` in editor code: exactly one** — `section-reorder.ts:51` on the handle itself (correct). In `global.css` the hits at 147, 376-377, 857, 5248 are on chrome/UI (`.twyne-page-spacer` at 376-377 is `pointer-events: none; user-select: none;`, the ruler at 5248-5250 is `user-select: none; touch-action: none;`). **None apply to `.ProseMirror` text.**
- **`pointer-events`**: no rule applies to `.ProseMirror` or its text. The relevant editor-adjacent ones are `.twyne-page-spacer { pointer-events: none }` (global.css:376), `.drag-overlay { pointer-events: none }` (1468), table resize handles (1067/1078/1097).

**Conclusion for §2:** nothing in CSS blocks dragging. The three real hazards are, in order: **the capture-phase `preventdefault:drop` on the scroll container**, **the unfiltered `.drag-overlay` re-render storm on every drag**, and **the invisible gap cursor**.

---

# 3. Scroll container & bottom-of-editor geometry

## Who scrolls

**Not the window.** A nested flex/overflow chain:

1. `src/routes/editor/index.tsx:937` — `<div class="editor-workspace-shell flex h-screen bg-[var(--color-paper)] overflow-hidden">`
2. `:1236` — `<div class="editor-workspace-main flex-1 flex flex-col min-w-0">`
3. `:1425` — `<div class="relative flex flex-1 min-h-0 overflow-hidden">` — *"The manuscript owns the remaining height beneath the masthead."*
4. `:1427` — `<div class="h-full min-w-0 flex-1 overflow-auto bg-[var(--color-paper-soft)]">` ← **outer scroller**, wraps `<TwyneEditor>`
5. `twyne-editor.tsx:3029` — `<div class="flex flex-1 flex-col min-h-0">`
6. `manuscript-panel.tsx:43` — `<div class="flex-1 overflow-y-auto overflow-x-auto">` ← **inner scroller** (the one with `preventdefault:drop`)
7. `manuscript-panel.tsx:65-87` — `.page-canvas.twyne-editor` (padding carrier)
8. `manuscript-panel.tsx:101-105` — `#twyne-editor-mount` → ProseMirror

There are **two nested `overflow:auto` containers** (steps 4 and 6). Step 4's child is `h-full`-less and the inner one is `flex-1`, so in practice #6 scrolls — but #4 is a live second scroller. `pagination.ts:421` calls `options.getScroller?.() ?? resolveScroller(view.dom)`, which walks up to whichever it finds first.

## Where height / padding is set

**Page canvas padding** (`manuscript-panel.tsx:74-86`):

```tsx
          style={{
            ...(store.paginationActive
              ? {
                  width: "var(--page-w)",
                  "flex-shrink": "0",
                  "min-height": `${props.canvasMinHeight}px`,
                }
              : { "max-width": "var(--doc-width, 48rem)" }),
            "padding-left": "var(--doc-pad-left, 3rem)",
            "padding-right": "var(--doc-pad-right, 3rem)",
            "padding-top": "var(--doc-pad-y, 2.5rem)",
            "padding-bottom": "var(--doc-pad-bottom, 4rem)",
          }}
```

**`--doc-pad-bottom` is written live** from `twyne-editor.tsx:436` (paginated) and `:451` (continuous):

```ts
root.style.setProperty("--doc-pad-bottom", `${m.bottom}rem`);
```

`m` comes from `resolveMargins(layout)` in `src/types/index.ts:402-411`:

```ts
    bottom: layout.marginBottom ?? (layout.margin === "roomy" ? 5 : 4),
```

But `DEFAULT_LAYOUT` (`src/types/index.ts:419-420`) overrides that fallback:

```ts
  marginTop: 1,
  marginBottom: 1,
```

**So in practice `--doc-pad-bottom` resolves to `1rem`, not the `4rem` CSS fallback.** The `4rem` default in the inline style never applies once the visible task runs. That alone accounts for "the empty space at the bottom disappeared" — 16px of bottom padding under the last line.

**Editor min-heights:**

```css
/* global.css:706 */
.twyne-editor .ProseMirror {
  outline: none;
  min-height: 60vh;
  ...
}

/* global.css:493 — paginated only */
.page-canvas.is-paginated .ProseMirror {
  min-height: var(--page-content-h, 60vh);
}
```

```ts
// twyne-editor.tsx:340 (useStyles$)
    .twyne-editor {
      min-height: 100%;
    }
```

**There is no scroll-past-end padding on the scroller itself.** Below the ProseMirror mount the only content is the conditional `.manuscript-notes` block (`manuscript-panel.tsx:108-151`, `mt-10 pt-6`), then the scroller ends. The colophon bar (`manuscript-panel.tsx:155-174`, `sticky bottom-0`) is a *sibling outside* the scroller, so it's a fixed footer row, not overlaying content.

`canvasMinHeight` (`twyne-editor.tsx:2529-2532`) only applies in paginated mode:

```ts
    const canvasMinHeight = () => {
      const g = computePageGeometry(store.layout, rootFontSize());
      return Math.max(0, store.pageCount * (g.pageH + g.gap) - g.gap);
    };
```

## Git history — was bottom space removed recently?

I checked the last 25 commits and `git log -p` over `global.css`, `manuscript-panel.tsx`, `twyne-editor.tsx`.

- Commit **`3c1de51` "refactor: simplify the writing workspace"** (Aug 14 2026) moved the scroller div out of `twyne-editor.tsx` into the new `manuscript-panel.tsx` **verbatim**. The diff shows the exact lines removed from one file and added to the other:
  ```
  -            class="flex-1 overflow-y-auto overflow-x-auto"
  -                    "min-height": `${canvasMinHeight()}px`,
  -              "padding-bottom": "var(--doc-pad-bottom, 4rem)",
  ```
  This was a pure extraction — no geometry change.
- `git log -S"preventdefault:dragover"` → only `cc51b65` (initial release) and `3c1de51` (the move). **The `preventdefault:drop` has been there since day one.** Same for `drag-overlay`.
- The only real bottom-space removals in history are old: `05f27a8` removed two `min-height: 100vh` and several `padding-bottom` rules — but on **legal/landing pages**, not the editor.
- `34fa49c` **added** `min-height: var(--page-content-h, 60vh)` and removed `margin-bottom: 0.85em` from a paragraph rule.

**No recent commit removed editor bottom padding.** The "no empty space at the bottom" is structural: `--doc-pad-bottom` = `1rem` from `DEFAULT_LAYOUT.marginBottom`, plus no scroll-past-end affordance on the scroller. Also note `global.css:719-722` sets `.twyne-editor .ProseMirror p { margin-bottom: 0.45em; }` — a tight trailing margin.

**Scroll APIs in play:**
```
src/components/editor/extensions/pagination.ts:453:   if (Math.abs(delta) > 1) scroller.scrollTop += delta;   // caret anchoring across repagination
src/components/editor/extensions/find-replace.ts:203,330,366:  tr.scrollIntoView()
src/components/editor/note-editing.ts:128:  editor.state.tr.setSelection(selection).scrollIntoView()
src/components/editor/document-outline.tsx:52:  element.scrollIntoView({ block: "center", behavior: "auto" })
src/components/editor/twyne-editor.tsx:1936 / 3382:  dom.scrollIntoView({ behavior, block: "center" })
```
**No `scrollMargin` or `scrollThreshold` is configured on the Editor anywhere** — PM's defaults (5px/0) apply, which with a 1rem bottom pad means the caret can sit flush against the bottom edge while typing.

---

# 4. CSS setup

- **Tailwind v4**, via `@tailwindcss/vite` (`vite.config.ts:5,26`).
- **One global stylesheet**: `/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/src/global.css` (~5600 lines), imported once at `src/root.tsx:18`. It opens with `@import "tailwindcss";` and defines the design tokens in an `@theme { }` block.
- Two scoped stylesheets: `src/components/editor/math/math.css` and `math/katex.min.css`.
- Some editor CSS is injected at runtime via Qwik `useStyles$` in `twyne-editor.tsx:339-378` (the `.twyne-editor { min-height: 100% }` + zen-mode rules).

Key editor rules verbatim (`src/global.css`):

```css
/* ── Tiptap manuscript page ──────────────────────────────── */
.twyne-editor .ProseMirror {          /* :706 */
